Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Document the security model, configuration, and streaming
 contract

Adds docs/SECURITY_HARDENING.md covering each boundary and why it is drawn where
it is, a full configuration reference, a worked multi-tenant example, and how to
verify a deployment from /api/capabilities. Adds SECURITY.md with a private
disclosure path and the deployment responsibilities that are configuration rather
than code.

Updates the README, which described behaviour the app no longer has. It now
documents the streaming endpoint with its event sequence, the OpenAPI contract, the
split health probes, and the configuration a multi-tenant deployment requires. The
security section previously offered generic advice such as "implement OAuth2 as
needed"; it now states what is enforced and what the operator must still set. The
roadmap drops items that have since shipped.
