+### POST /api/chat/stream
+Send a chat query and receive the answer incrementally as server-sent events.
+
+Events arrive in order: one `sources` event carrying grounding references, then `delta` events
+carrying incremental content, then one `done` event carrying the assembled response and its
+metadata. Concatenating every `delta` reproduces the final content exactly. Every event on a
+stream shares one `interactionId`, which is what feedback is posted against.
+
+```
+event: sources
+data: {"type":"sources","interactionId":"…","sources":[{"title":"OSHA Fall Protection",…}]}
+
+event: delta
+data: {"type":"delta","interactionId":"…","delta":"Fall protection triggers at 6 ft"}
+
+event: done
+data: {"type":"done","interactionId":"…","response":{"content":"…","processingTimeMs":842,…}}
+```
+
+An `error` event ends the stream when a request is refused after headers are committed — an
+exhausted quota, for example.
