+# Security policy
+
+## Reporting a vulnerability
+
+Report suspected vulnerabilities privately to **security@futurecontractorsofamerica.com**, or
+through GitHub's private vulnerability reporting on this repository. Please do not open a public
+issue for an unfixed vulnerability.
+
+A useful report includes the affected endpoint or component, the impact, and enough detail to
+reproduce it. We will acknowledge receipt, confirm or dispute the finding, and tell you when a fix
+ships.
+
+## Supported versions
+
+Fixes are issued against `main`. There are no maintained release branches.
+
+## Deployment responsibilities
+
+Some of the security properties of a deployment depend on how it is configured rather than on the
+code. Before treating an installation as production, read
+[docs/SECURITY_HARDENING.md](docs/SECURITY_HARDENING.md) — in particular:
+
+- `Auth:Enabled` is `false` by default. In that mode every caller is anonymous and shares one
+  storage partition, which is safe only for a single-tenant install.
+- Plan changes require `Billing:ProvisioningKey` or `Auth:AdminEmails`. Without either, upgrades
+  are refused rather than granted.
+- `X-Forwarded-For` is trusted only from proxies listed in `Network:KnownProxies`. Behind a load
+  balancer, per-caller rate limiting depends on configuring these.
+
+`GET /api/capabilities` reports the posture in effect and warns about each setting that leaves the
+deployment more open than recommended.
+
+## What is enforced in code
+
+- Default-deny authorization across the API when authentication is enabled.
+- Per-account partitioning of workspace files and conversation memory.
+- SSRF protection that validates resolved addresses on every redirect hop.
+- Isolation of retrieved web content before it reaches a tool-calling model.
+- Rate limiting partitioned per account, with a global backstop.
+- Fail-closed plan changes.
+
+Each has regression coverage in `Auricrux.Tests`, run on every push by the Security Scan workflow
+alongside a dependency audit, CodeQL, and secret scanning.
